message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Lares"
    given-names: "Ezequiel"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
title: "Cancer Research: Cross-Literature Analysis and Ferroptosis Simulation"
type: software
version: "2026-04"
date-released: "2026-04-23"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ELares/cancer_research"
abstract: >
  Open-source cancer research combining cross-literature analysis of
  4,830 research articles with Monte Carlo biochemical simulations of
  ferroptosis sensitivity across cell phenotypes, drug combinations,
  and tumor microenvironment features. A census layer covers the whole
  indexed cancer literature -- 4,403,994 MeSH-indexed articles and
  10,509,470 typed entity relations -- and is used to re-test the
  corpus-scale claims against articles the project did not select.
  Includes a reusable Rust simulation engine (ferroptosis-core) with
  Python bindings, a news source authentication pipeline, and a
  ~115-page book-format manuscript.
keywords:
  - cancer research
  - ferroptosis
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - cross-literature analysis
  - drug-tolerant persister cells
  - tumor microenvironment
  - sonodynamic therapy
  - open science
